This solution uses the interval tree to efficiently compute the LCP query, where the size of the string is `n`.

The `parse_query` function parses the query, extracting the sizes of the two sets and their elements.

The `calculate_lcp` function calculates the number of common characters between the two sets of elements.

The `solution` function parses the queries, initializes the segment tree, and performs the required query computations.

The `DefaultSeuqenceTreeFromPos` function creates a default sequence tree for the segment index, which supports queries based on positions.

